[IMG]https://files.catbox.moe/347t1s.png[/IMG]
ResourceWorldResetter schedules resource-world resets, evacuates players, regenerates through the matching world plugin, then verifies the result. Operators get status, history, and an admin GUI. Players get a teleport menu with permissions and reset-phase protection.

[IMG]https://files.catbox.moe/cja623.png[/IMG]
Install [B]exactly one[/B] platform JAR. The shared core is already included — do not install a separate rwr-core file.

[B]Spigot / CraftBukkit[/B]
[LIST]
[*]Install [B]RWR-Spigot-5.0.0.jar[/B]
[*]Requires [URL='https://modrinth.com/plugin/multiverse-core']Multiverse-Core 5.8.0+[/URL]
[*]Data folder: [B]plugins/ResourceWorldResetter/[/B]
[/LIST]

[B]Paper / Purpur / Folia[/B]
[LIST]
[*]Install [B]RWR-Paper-Folia-5.0.0.jar[/B]
[*]Requires [URL='https://modrinth.com/plugin/worlds-1']Worlds by TheNextLvl 4.4.0+[/URL]
[*]Data folder: [B]plugins/ResourceWorldResetter-Paper-Folia/[/B]
[*]This build does [B]not[/B] use Multiverse-Core. Multiverse-Core does not support Folia.
[/LIST]

[IMG]https://files.catbox.moe/nczm04.png[/IMG]
[LIST]
[*]Daily, weekly, monthly, and interval schedules with timezone-aware next-run calculation
[*]Configurable warning minutes and countdown broadcasts
[*]Safe player evacuation before regeneration
[*]Authoritative regeneration through Multiverse-Core or Worlds, then independent verification
[*]Crash journal that records interrupted operations without automatically repeating ambiguous resets
[*]Admin dashboard, world configuration, global settings, history, and confirmation screens
[*]Player teleport GUI with pagination, permissions, player counts, locked visibility, and reset-phase blocking
[*]Folia-safe scheduling and fully non-blocking player evacuation
[*]Public cancellable pre-reset and terminal post-reset events
[*]MiniMessage messages.yml
[/LIST]

[IMG]https://files.catbox.moe/j4bfr7.png[/IMG]
[LIST]
[*]Java [B]21+[/B]
[*]Minecraft API [B]1.21.4+[/B], including the [B]26.x[/B] server line
[*]The world plugin that matches the selected RWR build
[/LIST]

[IMG]https://files.catbox.moe/m4mpnm.png[/IMG]
[LIST]
[*][B]/rwr help[/B] — Permission-aware help
[*][B]/rwr status [id][/B] ([B]rwr.status[/B]) — Live reset / schedule status
[*][B]/rwr gui[/B] ([B]rwr.admin[/B]) — Admin configuration GUI
[*][B]/rwr tp[/B] ([B]rwr.tp[/B]) — Player teleport menu
[*][B]/rwr reset <id>[/B] ([B]rwr.reset[/B]) — Guarded immediate reset
[*][B]/rwr history [n][/B] ([B]rwr.history[/B]) — Recent reset history
[*][B]/rwr reload[/B] ([B]rwr.reload[/B]) — Transactional config reload
[/LIST]
[B]/rwr status [id][/B] is the single command for current phase and next-schedule information.

[IMG]https://files.catbox.moe/nwrda9.png[/IMG]
[LIST]
[*][B]rwr.admin[/B] (op) — Full admin GUI and admin actions
[*][B]rwr.reload[/B] (op) — Reload configuration
[*][B]rwr.reset[/B] (op) — Force a guarded reset
[*][B]rwr.status[/B] (op) — View status
[*][B]rwr.history[/B] (op) — View reset history
[*][B]rwr.tp[/B] (true) — Open the teleport GUI
[*][B]rwr.teleport.world.*[/B] (op) — Bypass per-destination teleport permissions
[/LIST]
Leave a destination [B]permission[/B] blank to make it public to anyone with [B]rwr.tp[/B]. Set it to any Bukkit node (for example a LuckPerms group) to restrict that destination.

[IMG]https://files.catbox.moe/tlbdkl.png[/IMG]
Back up the plugin data folder and managed worlds before upgrading. [B]v4.2.1 and earlier are legacy v4 releases.[/B] v5 uses a new configuration ([B]config-version: 5[/B]) and must be migrated manually. Install exactly one platform JAR, then run one supervised [B]/rwr reset <id>[/B] before enabling unattended resets.

